Pestilence was the killer of his previous incarnation, so he decided to
do him first to prove he had improved his skills. Some monsters started
zapping /oD at him, killing their comrades. Angels, resistant to most
of
his magic attacks, fell to his blessed +5 daggers. Unfortunately, he
didn't have the time to pick them up (unless he was going in that
general direction), and there were only 20 of them. Most of them were
spent fighting through the Pesty crowd and back (Pesty fell to +FoD).
Mind flayers and angels were teleported with the wands. DoubleF was
getting low on power (he was afraid of dropping the amulet to cast
spells because that would mean losing moves and the space to move to),
but he already made half the way to Famine's altar. He killed Famine
and
was at PW:11 and mobbed ~4 deep in a corridor, when he said to himself:
``No, I will not die this stupid way!''. He confused himself and read
one of his scrolls of charging, and it restored his powers to the
maximum.

